spec:
  grid: H x (3*H+2), H = 5 [observed]; solver enforces H == panel_w (square panels)
  structure: three H x H panels separated by two full-height divider columns of a single separator color
  colors:
    bg: 7 [observed]; solver auto-detects dominant color
    separator: 6 [observed]; appears only in the two divider columns
    content: two distinct non-bg colors, call them A and B
    panel_coloring: Left and Right use color A; Middle uses color B [observed]
  panels:
    each panel has 1-3 non-bg rows (at least 1); total across all three panels is 3-5 (must be <= H)
    each non-bg row uses exactly one content color (no mixing A and B in a single row)
    multi-row content blocks occupy contiguous rows
    content in each panel forms a single 4-connected component
    non-bg cells per row: 1-5
  output:
    single H x H panel; collect non-bg rows right-to-left by panel, top-to-bottom within panel
    stack collected rows at bottom of output, pad top with bg rows
    consecutive non-bg rows must share at least one column (4-connected vertically)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick H (use 5; generalize to 4-6 for variety)
    2. Choose bg, separator, and two content colors A, B (all distinct)
    3. Build the output panel (H x H) — decide total non-bg rows K in [3, H]
    4. Generate K non-bg rows; each row uses A or B (assign so that the eventual panel split is consistent)
    5. Place them bottom-aligned in the output; top H-K rows are bg
    6. Partition the K rows into three contiguous groups (for Right, Middle, Left — in that output order)
       ensuring each group has >= 1 row, group sizes sum to K, and each group is single-color
       with Left/Right using A and Middle using B
    7. Distribute groups into three panels: Right group -> Right panel, Middle group -> Middle panel,
       Left group -> Left panel; place each group at a random contiguous row offset within [0, H-groupsize]
    8. Assemble input: Left | sep_col | Middle | sep_col | Right
